    "summary": "The leading exponent of four-way independence in Afro-Cuban drumming. Plays clave with his left foot on a pedal cowbell, jam block or hi-hat while the right foot holds the bass line and the hands play bongo, timbale and conga parts across the kit. Rose with Gonzalo Rubalcaba's Proyecto, left Cuba in 1990, and became the engine of Latin and Latin-fusion records for Michel Camilo, Santana, Roy Hargrove, Chucho Valdés and many more."
  },
